WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:03.502
If the person who brings in your clients were gone tomorrow,

2
00:00:03.561 --> 00:00:05.941
how long would your business hold up?

3
00:00:07.041 --> 00:00:08.758
A business depends on people.

4
00:00:09.131 --> 00:00:12.299
Often, one or two of them bring in most of the revenue.

5
00:00:13.399 --> 00:00:15.512
With key person insurance, the business

6
00:00:15.512 --> 00:00:17.752
insures someone critical to its revenue.

7
00:00:18.055 --> 00:00:20.817
If that person dies or can no longer work,

8
00:00:20.876 --> 00:00:24.834
the money helps cover lost revenue and the cost of replacing them.

9
00:00:25.934 --> 00:00:29.416
For partners, life cover combined with a written agreement

10
00:00:29.510 --> 00:00:32.296
lets those who remain buy the share of the one who

11
00:00:32.296 --> 00:00:35.198
died from their family, without selling the business.

12
00:00:35.501 --> 00:00:37.833
The agreement is drawn up with a lawyer.

13
00:00:38.933 --> 00:00:41.963
A common mistake is protecting the staff but not

14
00:00:41.963 --> 00:00:45.400
the owners and key people, or partners with no written

15
00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:48.789
agreement on what happens if one of them dies.

16
00:00:49.889 --> 00:00:53.139
Start by identifying the key people, owners included.

17
00:00:53.442 --> 00:00:56.031
Gather what you already have, and check the tax

18
00:00:56.031 --> 00:00:58.723
side with your accountant before you decide.

19
00:00:59.823 --> 00:01:02.052
Read the business guide on avrastro.com,

20
00:01:02.052 --> 00:01:04.060
and go through it with an advisor.
